-- title:
--   No smaller universal collinear constant works
-- statement:
--   Fix an integer $n\ge2$. If a real number $K$ gives the selected whole-segment bound for every factored monic degree-$n$ polynomial with collinear root occurrences—namely $\mathrm{CollinearDiameterBound}(n,K)$—then $$\frac{1}{2^{n-1}\cos^n(\pi/(2n))}\le K.$$ The scaled Chebyshev family reaches this level on every adjacent gap, so changing the selected gap cannot lower the universal constant. This proves optimality in each degree, without classifying every equality configuration.
